      "side": 1,
      "message": "I should have looked a bit harder here, https://unicode.org/reports/tr51/#Emoji_Properties_and_Data_Files directly states \"Implementations must not, however, assume that all Emoji_Component characters are also Emoji.\" See https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/780558 . In general it isn\u0027t possible to look at a code point in isolation and determine if it should be \"emoji\" or not. Will most likely need to expose at least `isEmoji`, `isEmojiModifier`, and `isEmojiBase` and then have users of SkUnicode use these to figure out what to do. Also SkUnicode could provide a base implementation that takes a string and determines if it begins with an \"emoji\" run (and how long that run is).",
